# `from` on the right of `join`: removed by a certain fix (DS0152).
mode: syntax
---- query
from orders | join from customers on customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..48
  PIPELINE@0..47
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..11
      IDENT@5..11 "orders"
    WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
    PIPE@12..13 "|"
    WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
    JOIN_OP@14..47
      IDENT@14..18 "join"
      WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
      ERROR@19..23
        IDENT@19..23 "from"
      WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
      NAME_REF@24..33
        IDENT@24..33 "customers"
      WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
      IDENT@34..36 "on"
      WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
      NAME_REF@37..47
        IDENT@37..47 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@47..48 "\n"

error[DS0152]: `from` is not written after `join`
  --> query:1:20
  |
1 | from orders | join from customers on customerId
  |                    ^^^^ `join` takes a table directly
  |
  = help: remove `from`: `join customers`
  = note: a pipeline on the right goes in parentheses: `(from t | where x > 1)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from orders | join customers on customerId
which parses without errors
